notes               = "Untitled in source. DATE FLAG: printed ۱۳۷۲/۱/۱۶, which puts this page more than a year BEFORE its neighbours (153-155 are ۱۳۷۳, and page 157 is ۱۳۷۳/۴/۵) in a book that is otherwise 99% chronological. Either a typesetting slip for ۱۳۷۴ — which would be out of order the other way — or the book means it, as it did on pages 90 and 96-97. Transcribed and dated as printed; worth checking the folio again before this is trusted. 16 Farvardin = 5 April 1993. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben. Photo check 2026-07-31 (p156): the fatha is printed on the alef of اَبر — plausibly set to block the ezāfe misreading آبِ ابر — and the transcription's floating combining mark after آب has been re-attached accordingly (آب اَبر). The date line is printed ۱۳۷۲/۱/۱۶ exactly as transcribed: folio and date confirmed, the inversion is the book's own."
draft               = true

===persian===

من و درخت
بر خاک... و... در خاک
زمین را دوست داریم
و در این کهکشان...
همین را دوست داریم.
ابر،
روح آب است...
آب اَبر را نمی‌بیند... باور می‌کند...
ابر سطحِ باور را تر می‌کند...
۱۳۷۲/۱/۱۶

===machine===

The tree and I —
on the earth... and... in the earth,
we love the ground,
and in all this galaxy...
it is just this that we love.
The cloud
is the soul of the water...
The water does not see the cloud... it believes it...
The cloud wets the surface of belief...
1372/1/16

===lantern===

The tree and I,
on the earth and in the earth,
love the ground;
and in all this galaxy
it is just this that we love.
The cloud
is the soul of the water.
The water does not see the cloud — it believes it.
The cloud wets the surface of belief...

1372/1/16

===translation===

===footnotes===

The water cannot see the cloud it came from and will return to, so its relation to it is
belief rather than knowledge. The last line then makes belief a surface that rain can fall on.
